# systemd-sysusers snippet for steno-monitor (TECH_SPEC §10, T7.1).
#
# Install location: /usr/lib/sysusers.d/steno-monitor.conf (system) or
# /etc/sysusers.d/steno-monitor.conf (override). Run `systemd-sysusers`
# after install (the package post-install / Makefile install target should
# already do this; see README.md).
#
# The directive below creates a system user and group named
# "steno-monitor", with a locked password (no interactive login) and a
# fixed UID/GID range. Adjust UID/GID to match the deployment's site
# policy; keeping them fixed makes ownership of recordings and the SQLite
# database file deterministic across reinstalls.

u steno-monitor - "Steno service user" /var/lib/steno-monitor /usr/sbin/nologin
g steno-monitor -

# Notes:
#   - The home directory /var/lib/steno-monitor is created by tmpfiles.d
#     (see steno-monitor.tmpfiles) and chowned to steno-monitor.
#   - The recordings directory on USB must be chowned manually after the
#     mount is created, because sysusers cannot reach arbitrary mount
#     points reliably during first boot.
#   - Do NOT add the user to `audio` or `disk` groups; access to /dev/snd
#     and USB devices comes from the systemd unit's DeviceAllow= lines
#     (and, if needed, a udev rule that sets ACLs on /dev/snd/* for the
#     steno-monitor user).